.net&gt; Cc: Marc Zyngier &lt;marc.zyngier@arm.com&gt; Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/1431202014-3136-1-git-send-email-dev@lynxeye.de Signed-off-by: Thomas Gleixner &lt;tglx@linutronix.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 9cf82e72ec449b4516843377ac7a20abe300c64f)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47878 TEST=boot device, suspend/resume and video playback is ok CQ-DEPEND=CL:313083,CL:313085,CL:313086,CL:313087  Change-Id: I6ba9671d8bb994679686425abe5df4d916dbef63 Signed-off-by: Joseph Lo &lt;josephl@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313084 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="313084" owner_email="josephl@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/84/313084/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If7fbbb5692abf6bd0b6bda9d5861dd21739884ce" commit="ea6ddef99d974f62797f94727bfadebb16fa4342" commit_message="BACKPORT: genirq: Introduce irq_chip_set_type_parent() helper  This helper is required for irq chips which do not implement a irq_set_type callback and need to call down the irq domain hierarchy for the actual trigger type change.  This helper is required to fix further wreckage caused by the conversion of TI OMAP to hierarchical irq domains and therefor tagged for stable.  [ tglx: Massaged changelog ]  Signed-off-by: Grygorii Strashko &lt;grygorii.strashko@ti.com&gt; Cc: Sudeep Holla &lt;sudeep.holla@arm.com&gt; Cc: &lt;linux@arm.linux.org.uk&gt; Cc: &lt;nsekhar@ti.com&gt; Cc: &lt;jason@lakedaemon.net&gt; Cc: &lt;balbi@ti.com&gt; Cc: &lt;linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org&gt; Cc: &lt;tony@atomide.com&gt; Cc: &lt;marc.zyngier@arm.com&gt; Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # 4.1 Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/1439554830-19502-3-git-send-email-grygorii.strashko@ti.com Signed-off-by: Thomas Gleixner &lt;tglx@linutronix.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit b7560de198222994374c1340a389f12d5efb244a)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47878 TEST=boot device, suspend/resume and video playback is ok CQ-DEPEND=CL:313083,CL:313084,CL:313086,CL:313087  Change-Id: If7fbbb5692abf6bd0b6bda9d5861dd21739884ce Signed-off-by: Joseph Lo &lt;josephl@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/313085 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="313085" owner_email="josephl@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/85/313085/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3cf34eefb2120173855dcc634d96f4062664faad" commit="cb28844ea040d445c4fa352eb55ff5e57a3f2da6" commit_message="UPSTREAM: irqchip/tegra: Propagate IRQ type setting to parent  The LIC doesn't deal with the different types of interrupts itself but needs to forward calls to set the appropriate type to its parent IRQ controller.  Without this fix all IRQs routed through the LIC will stay at the initial EDGE type, while most of them should actually be level triggered.  Fixes: 1eec582158e2 &quot;irqchip: tegra: Add Tegra210 support&quot; Signed-off-by: Lucas Stach &lt;dev@lynxeye.de&gt; Cc: Stephen Warren &lt;swarren@wwwdotorg.org&gt; Cc: Thierry Reding &lt;thierry.reding@gmail.com&gt; Cc: Alexandre Courbot &lt;gnurou@gmail.com&gt; Cc: Jason Cooper &lt;jason@lakedaemon.net&gt; Cc: Marc Zyngier &lt;marc.zyngier@arm.com&gt; Cc: &lt;stable@vger.kernel.org&gt; # 4.1 Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/1445787552-13062-1-git-send-email-dev@lynxeye.de Signed-off-by: Thomas Gleixner &lt;tglx@linutronix.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 209da39154837ec1b69fb34f438041939911e4b4)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47878 TEST=boot device, suspend/resume and video playback is ok CQ-DEPEND=CL:313083,CL:313084,CL:313085,CL:313